
Welcome to Maze Linux — live and install medium.

The desktop runs as the live user `maze`; the text console (tty1) logs in as
`root`. Neither account has a password, and sudo needs none. Nothing you do
here is kept after a reboot.

To install Maze Linux:
  - Connect to the internet first: the network icon in the panel, or `nmtui` /
    `nmcli` in a terminal (Ethernet via DHCP connects automatically).
  - Then launch the graphical installer: the "Install Maze Linux" icon in the
    dock, or `maze-calamares`.

Get your bearings any time with:  mazelinux --welcome   (or --status / --help)

